{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh Rendering Component.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh Rendering Component.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mesh rendering component mesh rendering component","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh Rendering Component.md","fileName":"Mesh Rendering Component.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mesh Rendering Component","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-20 23:34\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[OpenGL Rendering Pipeline]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["OpenGL Rendering Pipeline","Game Actor","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh Rendering Component.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh Rendering Component.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mesh rendering component mesh rendering component","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh Rendering Component.md","fileName":"Mesh Rendering Component.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mesh Rendering Component","heading":"Mesh Rendering Component","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A mesh rendering component attaches a three-dimensional mesh and material behavior to a [[Game Actor]]. During drawing it supplies the actor's world transform, binds the required shader and textures, and submits the mesh's vertex array.\n\nSeparating mesh rendering from the actor lets the same actor architecture support different visual components. The mesh asset can also be cached and shared while each component retains its own owning actor and draw state.","tags":["baby"],"links":["OpenGL Rendering Pipeline","Game Actor","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh Rendering Component.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mesh Rendering Component.md","sourceType":"markdown","section